&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Klaviyo, we value the unique backgrounds, experiences and perspectives each Klaviyo (we call ourselves Klaviyos) brings to our workplace each and every day. We believe everyone deserves a fair shot at success and appreciate the experiences each person brings beyond the traditional job requirements. If you’re a close but not exact match with the description, we hope you’ll still consider applying. Want to learn more about life at Klaviyo? Visit &lt;a class=&quot;_ymio1r31 _ypr0glyw _zcxs1o36 _mizu194a _1ah3dkaa _ra3xnqa1 _128mdkaa _1cvmnqa1 _4davt94y _4bfu18uv _1hms8stv _ajmmnqa1 _vchhusvi _kqswh2mm _ect4ttxp _syaz13af _1a3b18uv _4fpr8stv _5goinqa1 _f8pj13af _9oik18uv _1bnxglyw _jf4cnqa1 _30l313af _1nrm18uv _c2waglyw _1iohnqa1 _9h8h12zz _10531ra0 _1ien1ra0 _n0fx1ra0 _1vhv17z1&quot; href=&quot;http://klaviyo.com/careers&quot; data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;klaviyo.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;to see how we empower creators to own their own destiny.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Senior Staff Engineer, Applied AI (Customer Agent)&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Engineering team builds the AI systems that power how brands run their businesses on Klaviyo. We move fast, ship in production, and hold a high bar for what &quot;AI-native&quot; actually means: systems that make real judgment calls, not demos.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Customer Agent team is one of the newest and most ambitious groups in that org, based in Boston and working in-office: we&#39;re building a conversational AI system that lets brands serve their own customers at a scale no human support team could match. We&#39;re still small enough that a single senior engineer can shape how the whole platform evolves. We&#39;re past the demo stage: the team ships changes against live customer traffic, measures quality with real evaluation frameworks, and treats reliability as a product feature, not an afterthought.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Senior Staff Engineer, you&#39;ll set technical and product direction for Customer Agent end to end, building a 0-to-1 agentic product with the speed and ownership of a startup, backed by the scale and resources of one of the most innovative tech companies on the East Coast, while staying hands-on with the hardest problems yourself. This is a principal-caliber individual contributor role: we&#39;re looking for an engineer who has personally architected, built, scaled, and supported a production agentic system through everything that comes after the demo, and who acts as a force multiplier across the org through the strength of their technical judgment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How You&#39;ll Make an Impact:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the technical and product direction for Customer Agent&#39;s core platform, from architecture through production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take on the platform&#39;s hardest technical problems personally: orchestration, evaluation, guardrails, memory &amp;amp; context, self-healing/improving and failure handling for non-deterministic systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write and ship code, review designs, and make the calls other engineers can&#39;t make alone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build architecture and frameworks that other engineers and teams adopt, and mentor through design reviews rather than direct management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product, design, data science, and go-to-market leaders to shape the roadmap, not just execute against it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate emerging AI technologies and bring the ones worth betting on into production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve architected, built, scaled, and supported a production agentic system end to end, not just prototyped one: real orchestration, evals, guardrails, and non-deterministic failure handling. You&#39;ve owned it through launch, scale, incidents, and the years of operational reality after the demo.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve learned the hard lessons that only come from running agents in production: securing them against misuse and abuse, and the operational scar tissue of keeping a non-deterministic system reliable as usage grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve set technical and product direction for an entire product area before, not just your own component, and you can point to something you designed and championed that shipped and that other teams built on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve stayed hands-on through all of it: still writing code, reviewing your own architecture decisions, and debugging production issues yourself, not delegating the hardest problems away.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your past architecture and frameworks got reused by other teams, and you&#39;ve unblocked multiple teams at once, not just your own.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You communicate complex technical trade-offs clearly across engineering, product, and executive audiences, and you can turn an undefined problem into a plan others rally behind.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Haves:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running a multi-tenant agent platform at production scale, where external customers configure their own agent behavior on shared infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building 0-to-1 products or working in startup environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record with production evaluation systems, AI observability, or human-in-the-loop workflows for LLM-powered products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Boston, MA – In-Office Role&lt;/p&gt;
